# Minimal operator evidence handoff

Read `docs/evidence/EVIDENCE_RETURN_PROTOCOL.md` and `docs/evidence/MINIMAL_OPERATOR_HANDOFF.md`.

- Never ask the operator to paste long terminal, test, diff or agent output into chat when repository evidence can be written and pushed.
- Store the complete packet return under `evidence/<packet-id>/<UTC-timestamp>/`.
- Create a short `OPERATOR_RETURN.md` with packet ID, status, branch, result SHA, evidence path, PR and one operator action.
- Redact secrets, personal data and unrestricted production identifiers.
- Commit and push the evidence on the packet branch when repository writes are authorized.
- Create or update the pull request and record the evidence path/result SHA there.
- Stop after the return; do not merge or start the successor.
- Do not require Google Drive access for the normal implementation loop. GitHub is the operational handoff; accepted outcomes are mirrored to Drive/Notion by Implementation Control.
